      "content": "For your Tokyo to Osaka and then Osaka to Fukuoka legs, the Shinkansen is generally the most reliable and often the most convenient choice, especially when you factor in airport travel time. While domestic flights are an option, they often involve the same logistical headaches as a trip to the nearest major airport, which can eat up time. I'd recommend sticking to the bullet train for a smooth, predictable journey, unless your schedule is so tight that you need to shave off every single minute, in which case you might compare flight times directly against the Shinkansen schedule.",
